# Examples: dashboard JSON (learning shape)

A Grafana dashboard for this project. Import into Grafana and read each panel.

```json
{
  "title": "shop-latency",
  "rows": [
    {
      "title": "App",
      "panels": [
        {
          "title": "RPS by endpoint",
          "targets": [
            {"expr": "sum(rate(http_request_duration_seconds_count[5m])) by (endpoint)", "refId": "A"}
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "p50 / p95 / p99 by endpoint",
          "targets": [
            {"expr": "histogram_quantile(0.50, sum(rate(http_request_duration_seconds_bucket[5m])) by (le, endpoint))", "legendFormat": "p50 {{endpoint}}"},
            {"expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum(rate(http_request_duration_seconds_bucket[5m])) by (le, endpoint))", "legendFormat": "p95 {{endpoint}}"},
            {"expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum(rate(http_request_duration_seconds_bucket[5m])) by (le, endpoint))", "legendFormat": "p99 {{endpoint}}"}
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Error ratio",
          "targets": [
            {"expr": "sum(rate(http_request_duration_seconds_count{status=~'5..'}[5m])) by (endpoint) / sum(rate(http_request_duration_seconds_count[5m])) by (endpoint)", "legendFormat": "5xx ratio {{endpoint}}"}
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "L7 (NGINX)",
      "panels": [
        {
          "title": "NGINX p95 by service",
          "targets": [
            {"expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum(rate(nginx_ingress_controller_request_duration_seconds_bucket[5m])) by (le, service, target))", "legendFormat": "{{service}} → {{target}}"}
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "DB",
      "panels": [
        {
          "title": "pg backends",
          "targets": [{"expr": "pg_stat_activity_numbackends", "legendFormat": "backends"}]
        },
        {
          "title": "pg_stat_statements mean exec (top 10)",
          "targets": [
            {"expr": "topk(10, pg_stat_statements_mean_exec_time)", "legendFormat": "{{queryid}}"}
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

## What to do with it

1. Import. Open. Read every panel out loud.
2. For each panel, write the **promql** in a notes file next to the panel.
3. Break the system (any break in `project/labs/break-the-system.md`) and predict *which panel moves first*.
4. Check your prediction. If wrong, that is the lesson.
